class:: SilenceRate
summary:: Fraction of recent RMS frames below an absolute threshold
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/DetectSilence

description::
Counts RMS frames at or below 10.pow(thresholdDB/20), divided by the observation frame count. Nonoverlapping frames and a complete-window warmup are used. Exact silence returns one after warmup. Thresholds may be arrays through multichannel expansion. Cost is linear in the frame count at each envelope update; memory is fixed at construction. This is an independent threshold-occupancy statistic.

Vanilla DetectSilence produces a state/action after sustained low level; SilenceRate describes how much of a rolling interval was quiet.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate input.

argument:: thresholdDB
Absolute RMS silence threshold, -160..0 dBFS.

argument:: windowTime
Literal window duration, 2*frameTime..10 seconds; default 0.5.

argument:: frameTime
Literal RMS frame duration, 0.001..0.1 seconds.

returns::
Fraction from zero through one.

examples::
SilenceRate tracks the proportion of rolling RMS envelope frames that fall below a specified decibel threshold (ranging from 0 for continuous sound to 1 for complete silence). In this example, when sparse playing leaves gaps of silence, SilenceRate automatically fades in an ethereal ambient drone pad, seamlessly filling the acoustic space. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time silence rate.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var silence = SilenceRate.kr(source, thresholdDB: -35, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var silLag = silence.lag(0.1);
        var drone = Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([110, 164.81, 220], 0, 0.05)) * silLag;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (drone ! 2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, silLag.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Silence Rate", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0, "ratio");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
